    "stipend_or_salary": "Competitive / Market standard",
    "description": "Job Description:\nRole:\nFull-Stack Engineer (Intern)\nCompany:\nSennovate Infotech (India) Pvt. Ltd\nJob Title:\nFull-Stack Engineer – Intern (Python / FastAPI & React / Next.js)\nExperience:\nFresher / 0–1 Year\nEmployment Type:\nInternship (Full-Time)\nWork Location:\nCoimbatore (On-Site)\nAbout the Role:\nWe are looking for enthusiastic and motivated Full-Stack Engineer Interns who are interested in building end-to-end enterprise web applications using\nPython (FastAPI)\n,\nPostgreSQL\n, and\nReact / Next.js\n.\nAs a Full-Stack Engineer Intern, you will work alongside experienced engineers to build and connect backend APIs, database models, real-time scan/telemetry views, and interactive dashboards for our enterprise AI Security & Governance Discovery platform.\nThis role is ideal for fresh graduates who enjoy owning features across both the backend and frontend and want real-world production experience.\nKey Responsibilities:\nAssist in building and maintaining REST and streaming (SSE) APIs using\nPython (FastAPI)\nand\nPydantic\n.\nWork with\nPostgreSQL\n,\nSQLAlchemy\n, and\nAlembic\nto support multi-tenant application features.\nBuild clean, responsive UI screens, interactive data tables, and graph/report views using\nNext.js\n,\nReact\n,\nTypeScript\n, and\nTailwind CSS\n.\nConnect frontend components to backend APIs cleanly through a typed API client with proper loading, error, and auth handling.\nWrite and maintain automated tests (pytest on the backend,\nPlaywright\n/ unit tests on the frontend).\nDebug integration issues across the UI, API, and database layers in containerized Linux environments.\nAssist in documenting API contracts, UI flows, and feature changes.\nRequired Technical Skills:\nCandidates should have basic knowledge or an understanding of the following:\n1. Frontend Development\nBasic hands-on experience with\nReact\nor\nNext.js\n, HTML, CSS, and\nJavaScript / TypeScript\n.\nFamiliarity with responsive layouts (Tailwind CSS or similar) and consuming REST APIs (fetch / HTTP status handling).\n2. Backend Development\nBasic hands-on experience in\nPython\nand building simple REST APIs (\nFastAPI\nor Flask).\nUnderstanding of JSON payloads, HTTP methods, and basic authentication concepts.\n3. Databases\nBasic knowledge of relational databases (\nPostgreSQL\nor SQLite) and writing SQL queries (SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, JOIN).\n4. Version Control & Operating Systems\nBasic knowledge of\nGit\nand\nGitHub\n(branching, commits, pull requests).\nBasic Linux/terminal comfort.\nGood to Have (Not Mandatory):\nHands-on experience with\nFastAPI\n,\nSQLAlchemy\n,\nNext.js App Router\n, or\nTailwind CSS\n.\nFamiliarity with\nPlaywright\n,\npytest\n, or Docker.\nExposure to graph visualization libraries (e.g., Cytoscape) or real-time updates (SSE/WebSockets).\nGitHub repositories demonstrating at least one full-stack project connecting a Python backend and SQL database to a React/Next.js frontend.\nEducational Qualification:\nB.E / B.Tech in Computer Science, Information Technology, or related disciplines.\nB.Sc / BCA / MCA or equivalent qualifications in Computer Science or IT.\n2025 / 2026 / 2027 graduates\nare welcome to apply.\nWhat We Expect From You:\nStrong interest in Full-Stack Engineering across Python backends and modern React/Next.js frontends.\nGood analytical and end-to-end debugging skills.\nWillingness to verify features from database to UI—including edge cases—before marking work complete.\nAbility to work independently and collaboratively within a team.\nGood communication and documentation skills.\nWhat You Will Gain:\nHands-on exposure to a modern production stack (\nFastAPI + PostgreSQL + Next.js 16 + TypeScript\n).\nPractical experience owning vertical feature slices from schema migration to UI and E2E testing.\nMentorship from experienced platform and security engineers.\nExposure to enterprise AI governance workflows, containerized deployments, and CI/CD quality gates.\nOpportunity to convert into a full-time\nJunior Full-Stack Engineer\nbased on performance and business requirements.\nImportant Note:\nThis is an entry-level internship opportunity. We do not expect candidates to be experts in all the technologies mentioned above. Candidates with strong fundamentals, genuine curiosity, and a willingness to learn are encouraged to apply.\nStart your journey in Full-Stack Engineering with Sennovate!",
