    "description": "Company Description\nKodeBinary Technologies is an Ahmedabad-based product and services company specialising in Telecom OSS and ISP platforms, AI-enabled network monitoring, cybersecurity, data centre and digital engineering services. Led by founders with over three decades of combined telecom and enterprise IT experience, KodeBinary delivers carrier-grade solutions with senior-led execution and measurable results.\nRole Description\nThe Engineer Intern role at KodeBinary Technologies is a full-time, on-site position based in Ahmedabad. The intern will support engineering teams in designing, developing, testing, and documenting software and technology solutions across areas such as web applications, enterprise systems, AI/ML components, and telecom platforms. Day-to-day responsibilities may include writing and reviewing code, assisting with integration and debugging, participating in technical discussions, and collaborating with senior engineers on features and enhancements. The role also involves conducting research on tools and technologies, preparing technical documentation, and contributing to proof-of-concept and pilot implementations. The intern will work closely with cross-functional teams to gain exposure to real-world projects and engineering best practices.\nQualifications\nFoundational programming skills in languages such as Java, Python, JavaScript, or similar, with the ability to write clean, maintainable code.\nBasic understanding of web and application development concepts, including front-end, back-end, APIs, and databases.\nFamiliarity with software engineering principles such as version control (e.g., Git), testing, debugging, and documentation.\nExposure to cloud platforms, AI/ML concepts, or telecom/enterprise systems is an advantage.\nStrong analytical and problem-solving abilities, with a willingness to learn new tools and technologies.\nEffective communication and collaboration skills, with the ability to work in a team-oriented environment on-site in Ahmedabad.\nCurrently pursuing or recently completed a degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Engineering, or a related technical field.\nInterest in building a career in software engineering, digital engineering, or technology product development.",
